<?php require __DIR__.'/../includes/bootstrap.php';$tool=tool_by_path('marketing','email-subject-line-analyzer');ob_start(); ?>
<h2>Check a subject line before you send</h2><p class="lead">Get transparent diagnostics for length, words, capitalization, punctuation and potentially promotional wording—without a fake “AI deliverability score.”</p><div class="field"><label for="subject">Email subject line</label><input id="subject" value="Quick question about your Q4 growth plan"></div><div class="result-box"><div class="result-grid"><div class="metric"><span>Characters</span><strong id="chars">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Words</span><strong id="words">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Uppercase letters</span><strong id="caps">0%</strong></div></div><div id="checks" style="margin-top:15px"></div></div>
<script>(()=>{const s=document.getElementById('subject'),$=i=>document.getElementById(i);const risky=['free','guaranteed','act now','urgent','winner','cash bonus','risk free','100%'];function go(){const v=s.value.trim(),w=v? v.split(/\s+/).length:0,letters=(v.match(/[a-z]/gi)||[]),upper=(v.match(/[A-Z]/g)||[]);$('chars').textContent=v.length;$('words').textContent=w;$('caps').textContent=letters.length?Math.round(upper.length/letters.length*100)+'%':'0%';const found=risky.filter(x=>v.toLowerCase().includes(x)),checks=[];checks.push([v.length>=25&&v.length<=60,'Length','25–60 characters is a practical mobile-friendly editing range, not a deliverability rule.']);checks.push([w>=4&&w<=10,'Word count','Four to ten words is a concise editing range for many messages.']);checks.push([letters.length===0||upper.length/letters.length<.4,'Capitalization','Heavy all-caps styling can feel aggressive and is harder to scan.']);checks.push([!/!{2,}|\?{2,}/.test(v),'Punctuation','Repeated exclamation or question marks can make a subject look noisy.']);checks.push([found.length===0,'Promotional phrases',found.length?'Review: '+found.join(', '):'No phrases from this small transparent review list were found.']);$('checks').innerHTML=checks.map(c=>`<div class="notice" style="margin:8px 0"><strong class="${c[0]?'success':'danger'}">${c[0]?'✓':'Review'} ${c[1]}</strong><br>${c[2]}</div>`).join('')}s.addEventListener('input',go);go()})();</script>
<?php $toolBody=ob_get_clean();ob_start(); ?>
<h2>What this analyzer actually checks</h2><p>The analyzer reports simple, inspectable signals: character count, word count, capitalization, repeated punctuation and matches against a small visible-style list of promotional phrases. It does not claim to predict inbox placement or open rate.</p><h2>How to improve a subject line</h2><ol><li>Make the main benefit, question or context clear early.</li><li>Remove filler words that do not help the recipient decide whether the message is relevant.</li><li>Avoid excessive capitalization and punctuation.</li><li>Match the promise in the subject with the email body.</li><li>Test variants with your actual audience rather than treating generic benchmarks as universal rules.</li></ol><h2>Why there is no deliverability score</h2><p>Inbox placement depends on sender reputation, authentication, complaint rates, engagement, list quality, content, provider filtering and other factors. A subject line alone cannot provide a scientifically valid deliverability percentage.</p><h2>Promotional wording requires context</h2><p>A word such as “free” is not automatically prohibited. The check simply flags wording worth reviewing for tone and accuracy; it is not a spam-filter simulator.</p>
<?php $toolContent=ob_get_clean();$faqs=[['Can a subject line analyzer predict open rate?','Not reliably from the subject alone. Audience, sender, timing, offer and inbox context all affect opens.'],['Does using the word free automatically send email to spam?','No. This tool flags promotional wording for review, but deliverability depends on many factors beyond individual words.'],['What subject length should I use?','There is no universal best length. Keep the main message clear early and test with your audience and device mix.'],['Does this tool send or store my subject line?','No. The analysis in this release runs in your browser.']];require __DIR__.'/../includes/tool-template.php';
